# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# API keys for the model provider layer.
#
#   cp .env.example .env   and fill in whichever you have.
#
# .env is gitignored. Never commit a real key. Keys are read from the
# environment only, are never written to a log, and are never included in an
# API response or an error message shown to the frontend.
#
# EVERY KEY HERE IS OPTIONAL. A provider whose key is missing is simply skipped
# in the fallback chain (config.yaml -> providers), not an error. You only get
# a hard failure when *every* provider in a chain is unavailable, and that
# error names each one and why it was passed over.
#
# With no keys at all the engine still runs end to end on the local providers
# (MiniLM embeddings + Ollama generation). `CCE_OFFLINE=1` forces that path
# explicitly - no network, no quota, no keys. That is what the test suite uses.
#
# Check what is actually live at any time:
#   python -m engine.providers.check
#   curl localhost:8000/health | jq .providers
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Groq -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generation. FREE tier, and comfortably the fastest hosted option.
# First entry in the default generation chain.
#   sign up: https://console.groq.com/keys
GROQ_API_KEY=

# --- Google (Gemini) --------------------------------------------------------
# BOTH roles: embeddings (text-embedding-004) and generation (gemini-2.0-flash).
# FREE tier with a generous daily quota. One key covers both.
#   sign up: https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
GOOGLE_API_KEY=

# --- Cohere -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Embeddings (embed-english-v3.0). FREE trial key, rate-limited but generous.
#   sign up: https://dashboard.cohere.com/api-keys
COHERE_API_KEY=

# --- OpenAI -----------------------------------------------------------------
# BOTH roles: embeddings (text-embedding-3-small, ~$0.02/1M tokens) and
# generation (gpt-4o-mini). PAID - no free tier - but the cheapest high-quality
# baseline, and the default stage-3 embedding provider. Also used by the
# optional LLM-as-judge in the eval harness.
#   sign up: https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# --- OpenRouter -------------------------------------------------------------
# Generation, routed to any model you name. FREE for `:free`-tagged models.
# Not in the default chain; add `openrouter` to providers.generation_providers
# in config.yaml to use it.
#   sign up: https://openrouter.ai/keys
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# Which models carry the `:free` tag changes month to month, so override the
# config default here rather than editing code.
# OPENROUTER_MODEL=meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct:free

# --- local-only switch ------------------------------------------------------
# Set to 1 to collapse both chains to their local providers and make no network
# calls at all. Useful for offline demos and required by the unit tests.
# CCE_OFFLINE=1
